    {
      "id": "seg:paragraph:discussion:0010:0002",
      "blockId": "paragraph:discussion:0010",
      "type": "sentence",
      "source": "If the peer process initiated the connection and its executable doesn’t satisfy the lightweight code requirement, then you don’t receive a message and the operating system doesn’t call your event handler.",
      "normalizedSource": "If the peer process initiated the connection and its executable doesn’t satisfy the lightweight code requirement, then you don’t receive a message and the operating system doesn’t call your event handler.",
      "sourceHash": "46c4d1b9f306b57f6935e2d2f5595b9bc5dd1873d9ad21a977d83c1d3eafe61d",
      "translatable": true,
      "contextBefore": "When you set this requirement on a connection, the operating system checks that peer process satisfies the requirement every time it sends a message to your process.",
      "contextAfter": "If your process sent a message to its peer expecting a reply, and its executable doesn’t have the requested entitlement, then you don’t receive a reply and the operating system delivers [`XPC_ERROR_PEER_CODE_SIGNING_REQUIREMENT`](xpc_error_peer_code_signing_requirement-c.macro.md) instead.",
      "documentTitle": "xpcconnectionsetpeerplatformidentityrequirement(::)",
      "framework": "XPC",
      "ko": "",
      "status": "failed",
      "reviewed": false,
      "locked": false
    },
    {
      "id": "seg:paragraph:discussion:0010:0003",
      "blockId": "paragraph:discussion:0010",
      "type": "sentence",
      "source": "If your process sent a message to its peer expecting a reply, and its executable doesn’t have the requested entitlement, then you don’t receive a reply and the operating system delivers [`XPC_ERROR_PEER_CODE_SIGNING_REQUIREMENT`](xpc_error_peer_code_signing_requirement-c.macro.md) instead.",
      "normalizedSource": "If your process sent a message to its peer expecting a reply, and its executable doesn’t have the requested entitlement, then you don’t receive a reply and the operating system delivers [`XPC_ERROR_PEER_CODE_SIGNING_REQUIREMENT`](xpc_error_peer_code_signing_requirement-c.macro.md) instead.",
      "sourceHash": "1f4a18492faafa0ec5bf08f8d3092d6094201e3b6cd0eddd5d95268f00350080",
      "translatable": true,
      "contextBefore": "If the peer process initiated the connection and its executable doesn’t satisfy the lightweight code requirement, then you don’t receive a message and the operating system doesn’t call your event handler.",
      "contextAfter": "❗ **Important**: It’s an error to call this function multiple times for the same connection, or to call multiple functions that set code-signing requirements on the same connection.",
      "documentTitle": "xpcconnectionsetpeerplatformidentityrequirement(::)",
      "framework": "XPC",
      "ko": "",
      "status": "failed",
      "reviewed": false,
